An electronic display device comprising:

a liquid crystal display panel including a plurality of display elements arranged in a matrix having a plurality of rows and a plurality of columns;

a plurality of scan lines respectively corresponding to the plurality of rows, each scan line being configured to select display elements in a corresponding row;

a plurality of signal lines respectively corresponding to the plurality of columns, each signal line being configured to supply image signals to display elements in a corresponding column;

a plurality of touch detection electrodes respectively corresponding to the plurality of columns; and

a touch controller configured to select at least one touch detection electrode from among the plurality of touch detection electrodes,

wherein a touch drive signal is supplied only to the touch detection electrode selected by the touch controller.

In one embodiment, the touch controller sequentially selects the touch detection electrodes to perform touch detection in a column-by-column manner.

In another embodiment, touch detection is performed by applying the touch drive signal to the selected touch detection electrode while non-selected touch detection electrodes are not supplied with the touch drive signal.

In another embodiment, the touch detection electrodes are disposed so as to extend in a column direction of the liquid crystal display panel and are arranged in correspondence with the signal lines.
